@startuml use-case-overview
title ADMS - Use Case Overview (system context)
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest\n(unauthenticated client)" as Guest
actor "Staff User\n(authenticated, role=USER)" as Staff
actor "Superadmin\n(role=SUPERADMIN)" as Super

Staff --|> Guest
Super --|> Staff

rectangle "ADMS Backend" {
  usecase "Authenticate\n(login / logout)" as UC_Auth
  usecase "Manage Users\n& Access" as UC_Users
  usecase "Manage Items" as UC_Items
  usecase "Manage Warehouses" as UC_Warehouses
  usecase "Manage Companies" as UC_Companies
  usecase "Manage Tenders" as UC_Tenders
  usecase "Manage Organization\nSettings" as UC_Org
  usecase "Generate & View\nStock Reports" as UC_Reports
}

Guest --> UC_Auth
Guest --> UC_Users
Guest --> UC_Items
Guest --> UC_Warehouses
Guest --> UC_Companies
Guest --> UC_Tenders
Guest --> UC_Org
Guest --> UC_Reports

note right of UC_Users
  Guest: register the very first
  account (bootstrap) + view/rename
  any user. Superadmin adds: create
  further users, change roles,
  grant/revoke permissions, delete.
end note

note right of UC_Reports
  Guest/Staff/Superadmin can all view
  past reports; generating a **new**
  report requires any authenticated
  session (Staff or Superadmin).
end note

note bottom of UC_Items
  Items, Warehouses, Companies, Tenders
  and Organization Settings currently
  have **no authentication check** at
  all - every operation shown for
  Guest is reachable by any client.
  See the detailed per-module diagrams
  in use-case-details.puml for the
  full breakdown.
end note

legend bottom
  This is the high-level context diagram. For the full set of
  use cases inside each box above, see the matching diagram
  in **use-case-details.puml**.
endlegend

@enduml
